===========================================
💎 ACID PROPERTIES — MASTER NOTES (FAANG LEVEL)
===========================================

🔥 FIRST PRINCIPLE (WHY ACID EXISTS?)
-------------------------------------
👉 Real world = unreliable
   - Power failure ⚡
   - Concurrent users 👥
   - System crash 💥

👉 Without ACID:
   - Data corrupt 😵
   - Money loss 💸
   - Inconsistent DB

💡 ACID ensures:
👉 "Database is ALWAYS correct & reliable"


===========================================
🧠 WHAT IS A TRANSACTION?
-------------------------------------------
👉 A group of operations treated as ONE unit

Example:
Transfer ₹100 from A → B

Steps:
1) Debit A
2) Credit B

👉 This MUST behave as ONE unit


===========================================
1️⃣ ATOMICITY (ALL OR NOTHING 💣)
===========================================

🧠 INTUITION:
-------------
👉 Either EVERYTHING happens OR NOTHING happens

-------------------------------------

💥 EXAMPLE:
-------------------------------------
A = ₹1000, B = ₹500

Transfer ₹100:

Step 1: A = ₹900 ✅
Step 2: B = ₹600 ❌ (crash here)

👉 BAD STATE 😱

-------------------------------------

💡 ATOMICITY GUARANTEE:
-------------------------------------
👉 If any step fails:
   Rollback EVERYTHING

Final:
A = ₹1000
B = ₹500

-------------------------------------

⚙️ HOW IT IS IMPLEMENTED:
-------------------------------------

👉 Write Ahead Log (WAL)

Example log:
[START TRANSACTION]
[DEBIT A -100]
[CREDIT B +100]
[COMMIT]

👉 If crash before COMMIT:
   → Undo all changes

👉 If crash after COMMIT:
   → Redo from log

-------------------------------------

🌍 REAL WORLD:
-------------------------------------
👉 Payment systems (UPI, banking)
👉 E-commerce checkout

-------------------------------------

⚠️ COMMON MISTAKE:
-------------------------------------
❌ People think partial success is okay
✔️ DB says: NO PARTIAL STATE


===========================================
2️⃣ CONSISTENCY (VALID STATE ALWAYS ✅)
===========================================

🧠 INTUITION:
-------------
👉 DB must follow ALL rules/invariants

-------------------------------------

📌 WHAT ARE INVARIANTS?
-------------------------------------
👉 Rules like:

✔️ Balance ≥ 0
✔️ Foreign key valid
✔️ Unique constraints

-------------------------------------

💥 EXAMPLE:
-------------------------------------

Before:
Total money = ₹1500

After transfer:
Still ₹1500 ✅

👉 No money created/destroyed

-------------------------------------

💡 CONSISTENCY GUARANTEE:
-------------------------------------
👉 Transaction moves DB:
VALID STATE → VALID STATE

-------------------------------------

⚙️ HOW IT IS IMPLEMENTED:
-------------------------------------

1) Constraints:
   - Primary key
   - Foreign key
   - Unique

2) Application logic

-------------------------------------

⚠️ IMPORTANT INSIGHT:
-------------------------------------
👉 DB ensures constraints
👉 Developer ensures business logic

-------------------------------------

🌍 REAL WORLD:
-------------------------------------
👉 Airline booking:
   Seat count cannot go negative

👉 Inventory system:
   Stock cannot be < 0


===========================================
3️⃣ ISOLATION (NO INTERFERENCE 🧱)
===========================================

🧠 INTUITION:
-------------
👉 Multiple transactions act like they run alone

-------------------------------------

💥 PROBLEM:
-------------------------------------

User1: Book seat S1
User2: Book seat S1

👉 Without isolation:
   BOTH may get same seat 😱

-------------------------------------

💡 ISOLATION GUARANTEE:
-------------------------------------
👉 No race conditions
👉 No dirty reads

-------------------------------------

⚠️ ANOMALIES (VERY IMPORTANT)
-------------------------------------

1️⃣ DIRTY READ:
-------------------------------------
👉 Read uncommitted data

Example:
T1 updates balance → NOT committed
T2 reads it → WRONG

-------------------------------------

2️⃣ NON-REPEATABLE READ:
-------------------------------------
👉 Same query → different result

-------------------------------------

3️⃣ PHANTOM READ:
-------------------------------------
👉 New rows appear suddenly

-------------------------------------

🔒 ISOLATION LEVELS:
-------------------------------------

1) Read Uncommitted ❌
2) Read Committed
3) Repeatable Read
4) Serializable (Strongest 💪)

-------------------------------------

⚙️ HOW IMPLEMENTED:
-------------------------------------

👉 Locks (pessimistic)
👉 MVCC (optimistic)

-------------------------------------

🌍 REAL WORLD:
-------------------------------------
👉 Ticket booking systems
👉 Stock trading systems


===========================================
4️⃣ DURABILITY (DATA NEVER LOST 💾)
===========================================

🧠 INTUITION:
-------------
👉 Once committed → ALWAYS saved

-------------------------------------

💥 PROBLEM:
-------------------------------------
👉 System crash after payment

👉 Without durability:
   Payment gone 😱

-------------------------------------

💡 DURABILITY GUARANTEE:
-------------------------------------
👉 After COMMIT:
   Data survives crashes

-------------------------------------

⚙️ HOW IMPLEMENTED:
-------------------------------------

1) WAL (Write Ahead Log)
   → Always written to disk first

2) Disk persistence

3) Replication (advanced systems)

-------------------------------------

🌍 REAL WORLD:
-------------------------------------
👉 Banking transactions
👉 Order confirmations

-------------------------------------

⚠️ IMPORTANT:
-------------------------------------
👉 Memory ≠ durable
👉 Disk = durable


===========================================
⚔️ INTERVIEW COMPARISON SUMMARY
===========================================

| Property    | Meaning                  | Focus             |
|------------|--------------------------|-------------------|
| Atomicity  | All or nothing           | Failure handling  |
| Consistency| Valid state              | Rules/invariants  |
| Isolation  | No interference          | Concurrency       |
| Durability | Never lost after commit  | Persistence       |

===========================================
🧠 DEEP INSIGHTS (INTERVIEW GOLD 🔥)
===========================================

👉 Atomicity + Durability = WAL magic

👉 Isolation = hardest problem in DB

👉 Consistency ≠ same as CAP consistency
   (VERY IMPORTANT CONFUSION)

-------------------------------------

🔥 GOLDEN LINE:
-------------------------------------
👉 ACID = correctness under failures + concurrency


===========================================
⚠️ REAL WORLD TRADEOFFS
===========================================

👉 Strict ACID → slower systems

👉 Modern systems:
   - Relax isolation (eventual consistency)
   - Use BASE instead of ACID

-------------------------------------

Example:
👉 NoSQL DBs sacrifice strict ACID


===========================================
🔥 FINAL ANALOGY (SUPER IMPORTANT)
===========================================

Transaction = Online Shopping 🛒

Atomicity:
👉 Either full order placed or nothing

Consistency:
👉 Stock & payment correct

Isolation:
👉 No one steals your item mid-checkout

Durability:
👉 Order stays even after crash

